Lab 2: Automated Deep Learning Model Training with CI/CD
Objective
Set up a local version control system using Git and integrate Jenkins for continuous integration and deployment (CI/CD), automating the training of a deep learning model on your Ubuntu machine.

Prerequisites
Start your Al Nafi-provided Ubuntu machine

Ensure the following tools are installed:

Git: sudo apt install git -y

Python3 & pip (should already be installed)

Jenkins

Java (for Jenkins): sudo apt install default-jre -y

Steps
Step 1: Set Up a Git Repository
Create a directory for your model project:

mkdir -p ~/dl-cicd-lab/model-training
cd ~/dl-cicd-lab/model-training
Initialize a Git repository:

git init
Add a simple training script (train.py):

cat > train.py <<EOF
from sklearn.datasets import load_iris
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier
import joblib

iris = load_iris()
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(iris.data, iris.target, test_size=0.2)

model = RandomForestClassifier()
model.fit(X_train, y_train)

print("Model trained. Accuracy:", model.score(X_test, y_test))
joblib.dump(model, "iris_model.pkl")
EOF
Add and commit your files:

git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit with training script"
Step 2: Install and Start Jenkins
Install Jenkins:

sudo apt install jenkins -y
Start and enable Jenkins:

sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins
Get the initial admin password:

sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
Open Jenkins in your browser:
http://localhost:8080
Log in and complete the setup (install suggested plugins).

Step 3: Configure Jenkins Job for Model Training
In Jenkins, create a new Freestyle Project named Model_Training_Pipeline.

Under Source Code Management, choose Git and enter your local repo path (e.g., /home/ubuntu/dl-cicd-lab/model-training).

Under Build, add a Build Step:

Choose Execute shell

Add the command to run the training script:

python3 train.py
Save and run the job.

Conclusion
In this lab, you:

Created a Git repository to manage deep learning code

Installed and configured Jenkins for automation

Set up a CI/CD pipeline to automatically train a model upon each commit or trigger

This simulates how CI/CD improves reproducibility, automation, and reliability in deep learning workflows — all on your local machine without any cloud dependency.
